reduces manual effort, accelerates response times, and enables scalable IT operations.', 9, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"tag":"h4","type":"heading","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The Role of Automation in IT Managed Services: From Reactive Support to Intelligent Operations","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"At 2:13 AM, a storage threshold is breached.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"In a traditional IT setup, that alert waits until someone notices it. A ticket gets raised. An engineer investigates. The issue escalates. Hours pass. Users feel the impact.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"In a modern IT environment, that same alert can trigger an automated response within seconds. Capacity gets reallocated, a remediation script runs, the right teams are notified, and business operations continue without disruption.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"That difference is not about having more engineers. It''s about automation.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"As enterprise IT environments become more distributed, complex, and always-on, manual operating models are struggling to keep pace. Bus